~ A deferred value stored into a top-level `:=` binding (see docs/concurrency/README.md).
~ `crackOpen` stores `io.@readStdin()`'s deferred Text into the global `fortune` and
~ returns `$` without ever reading it — the store itself never waits. `^`, a separate
~ function, then reads `fortune`: that read is where the value is finally forced.

<< core.io

fortune := ""
crackOpen = () -> $ => < fortune := io.@readStdin() >

^ = () -> Num => <
  crackOpen()
  io.print(fortune)                                       ~ FORCES the stored read
  assert(fortune, equals("you will fix a bug that does not exist yet"))
  0
>
